      "locality": [
        {
          "name": "Bridgetown",
          "isWeedLegalHere": {
            "overview": [
              {
                "_key": "a70b54cdcda1",
                "_type": "block",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_key": "a212e6c758610",
                    "_type": "span",
                    "marks": [],
                    "text": "In Bridgetown, Barbados, cannabis is illegal for recreational use but has been decriminalized for small amounts. Possession of up to 14 grams of cannabis or ganja can result in a $200 fine, with no criminal charges typically imposed. However, the law remains strict, especially for young individuals caught with marijuana, who may be referred to drug abuse programs or community service. Despite recreational cannabis being illegal, Barbados legalized medical cannabis in November 2019 through the Medicinal Cannabis Industry Bill, allowing registered Rastafarians to use cannabis for spiritual purposes under the Sacramental Cannabis Bill."
                  }
                ],
                "markDefs": [],
                "style": "normal"
              },
              {
                "_key": "9036e52fcea3",
                "_type": "block",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_key": "5ad685dd1eae0",
                    "_type": "span",
                    "marks": [],
                    "text": "When it comes to cannabis derivatives in Bridgetown, Barbados, Delta-8 and Delta-9 THC, along with THCA and CBD, play significant roles. Delta-8 THC is considered a milder version of Delta-9 THC and exists in a legal gray area in some regions. THCA is non-psychoactive and requires less caution in dosing compared to THC. Understanding the legal landscape around these compounds is crucial due to the complexities of regulations governing their sale and use, especially considering the differences between natural cannabinoids and synthetic versions like THC-O."
                  }
                ],
                "markDefs": [],
                "style": "normal"
              }
            ],
